ness Administration Full Time, Tenure Track, Biology Faculty Administrative Campus IT Support Specialist Major Gift/Enrollment Officer Staff Chellie Club and Spirit Shop Manager (Part-Time) Custodian Athletics Assistant Athletic Trainer Additional Resources Employee Benefit Guide Administrative Employee Handbook Hourly Employee Handbook Notice of Availability of the Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Additional Information Cottey College is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing equal opportunity to its students and employees in all aspects of campus life. The College does not unlawfully discriminate in educational programs, recruitment and admissions of applicants, school-administrated activities or programs, or employment opportunities, policies, or practices on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other status protected by law. In addition, and in accordance with Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Cottey College does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs, school-administrated activities or programs, or employment opportunities, policies, or practices. Cottey College has designated Title IX coordinators to handle all inquiries regarding its efforts to comply with and carry out its responsibilities under Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972. Unless otherwise noted in a specific listing, all faculty and academic affairs staff inquiries and applications should be directed to: Office of Academic Affairs Cottey College 1000 W. Austin Nevada, MO 64772 The phone number for the office is (417) 667-8181, ext. 2128. acadaffairs@cottey.edu All administrative and staff inquiries and applications should be directed to: Human Resources -Kelly Irvin Cottey College 1000 W. Austin Nevada, MO 64772 (417) 667-8181, ext. 2103 kirvin@cottey.edu Apply to Cottey Campus Map Emergency Employment & Jobs Policies and Privacy Marketing & Communications Consumer Information Campus Directory Single-Sex Admission Policy Cottey College 1000 W. Austin Blvd. Nevada, MO 64772 (417) 667-8181 Admission: admit@cottey.edu Back to top © 2026 Copyright Cottey College. All Rights Reserved."
